lines=['# Form Five History — learning path','','Each opening states an outcome, earlier knowledge and next use. Practice sources are explicitly invented; real historical proof requires authentic evidence.','','| Row | Topic | By the end | Builds on | Leads to |','|---|---|---|---|---|']
lines += [f'| {n} | {title} | {goal} | {back} | {onward} |' for n,title,goal,back,onward in sorted(PATH)]
lines += ['','All seventeen Term One lesson rows are active drafts. Rows 1/2 select Ghana/Nigeria as explicit case studies under the broad sheet titles; confirm these choices with teachers. Repeated/continued rows develop different aspects rather than duplicating an earlier lesson.','','Overall destination: explain change through actors, institutions and conditions; read sources within their limits; distinguish sovereignty, membership, cooperation and outcomes.']
(OUT/'LEARNING-PATH.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
(OUT/'TEACHER-REVIEW.md').write_text('''# Form Five History — teacher review

- TR-history-1: Confirm Ghana and Nigeria for the broad unnamed decolonisation case-study rows 1/2. The choices are explicit; no spine titles were silently corrected.
- TR-history-2: Confirm depth and accepted interpretations of West African constitutional stages, Guinea’s No vote and colonial perspectives. No claim that Guinea was the first independent African state is taught. OIF/official pages can contain errors; source status is not a guarantee of every sentence’s accuracy.
- TR-history-3: Rows 4/5 concern the early Congo crisis, not all later DRC wars. Verify treatment of colonial institutions, secession, foreign interests, leadership violence and ONUC’s changing mandate. Avoid a single-cause or essentialist explanation. ONUC establishment uses the Security Council resolution’s 14 July 1960 action date; a retired US overview gives 13 July and is not followed for that date.
- TR-history-4: Distinguish Guinea-Bissau’s 1973 declaration from Portuguese recognition in 1974. Portuguese official historical accounts are also viewpoints; confirm liberation movements, negotiated stages and post-independence conflicts.
- TR-history-5: Verify local syllabus treatments of instability/coups and avoid treating ethnicity or independence as inevitable causes. The invented army-council statement is not an actual coup proclamation.
- TR-history-6: Confirm the 1870–1914 thematic scope, earlier roots of innovations and uneven access. Industrialisation/Depression lessons do not make universal claims about welfare, policy success or recovery timing.
- TR-history-7: Confirm CEMAC institutional terminology and local dated examples of setbacks. Model obstacles are invented, not current border rules, travel conditions or official trade statistics.
- TR-history-8: UN admission is 20 September 1960, although the collected resolution’s publication metadata is 1961. Distinguish OAU founding membership from AU succession and EU partnership from membership.
- TR-history-9: OIF country profile distinguishes 1975 association/1991 participation, while an older status table lists 1975 as membership. No single disputed OIF accession date is assessed; confirm the school’s convention. Commonwealth accession is sourced as 1 November 1995.
- TR-history-10: Cameroon is not an Arab League member. Confirm the specific historical League-related cooperation examples expected by the sheet; bilateral Arab-state ties are not automatically League programmes. The draft provides the institutional distinction without inventing a project.
- TR-history-11: Major-power references are dated: historical US recognition, Soviet/Russian succession and the 1971 China communiqué. The communiqué is a primary document reproduced in a historical periodical mirror. No current officeholder, funding total or guaranteed project outcome is asserted.
- TR-history-12: Every practice source says invented/not an archive quotation. Teachers should supply authentic extracts for deeper source criticism and verify accepted alternative explanations. Technical checks are not teacher approval or evidence of real learning.
''',encoding='utf-8')
assert len(PATH)==17 and {n for n,*_ in PATH}==set(range(1,18))
